@@ -6,3 +6,14 @@ package holds the order book, in TypeScript; the shop's website and its staff to
 `src/index.ts`.
 
 Prices are integer cents everywhere. Run the tests with `npm test`.
+
+## Discount codes
+
+`orders.applyCode(orderNumber, code)` gives an order a discount code and returns its new totals; one code per order,
+a second replaces the first, and a refused code leaves the order as it was.
+
+- `SPRING10`: 10 % off the items, rounded to the nearest cent (half a cent rounds up).
+- `WELCOME5`: 5.00 € off the items, only when the items come to 30.00 € or more.
+
+`totals` shows the discount as `discountCents`; `totalCents` is items minus discount plus shipping. The discount never
+touches shipping, and free shipping is decided on the items before any discount.
